SUMMARY:What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**For Nov 12 thru Nov 18**\nUpcoming **musi
 c events** may be found here:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/\n(
 Updates on Thurs morning)\n.\n**Assorted entertainment\, festival & market
  events may be found here:**\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/calendar-o
 f-events\n.\n**Library programs** may be found here:\nhttps://hendersonpl.
 libcal.com/\n.\n**Every Thursday\; Nov 12**\nCountry Line Dance Lesson\n7-
 9pm\, Honeysuckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\, Hendersonville NC 28792\nCo
 st: $5 per person.\n.\n**Every Friday\; Nov 13**\nCountry Dance Lesson - S
 tyle Varies\n7-8pm\, Honeysuckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\, Hendersonvil
 le NC 28792\nCost: $5 per person.\n.\n**November 12 - November 18**\nOur T
 own – An Art Exhibition\nat Art MoB Studios\nhttps://visithendersonville
 nc.org/event/our-town-an-art-exhibition-celebrating-henderson-county\nhttp
 s://www.artmobstudios.com/\n.\n**Nov 12 thru Dec 20\;** Event Times: 2:00 
 PM & 7:30 PM\; $$$\nA Flat Rock Playhouse Christmas Show – 10th Annivers
 ary Special\nhis year’s festivities are stuffed fuller than Santa’s sl
 eigh with the songs you can’t wait to hear — the holiday hits and belo
 ved carols you ask for every year\, delivered with fa-la-la flair and show
 -stopping shine.\nJoin us for a spectacular celebration that is wrapped in
  joy\, tied with tradition\, and topped with a bow of pure Playhouse magic
 .\nFlat Rock Playhouse\; 2661 Greenville Hwy\, Leiman Mainstage\nhttps://v
 isithendersonvillenc.org/event/a-flat-rock-playhouse-christmas-show-10th-a
 nniversary-special/2026-12-06\nhttps://purchase.flatrockplayhouse.org/over
 view/4120\n\,\n**November 14** @ 10:00 am - 4:00 pm\; $5.00\nSouthern Touc
 h Craft Show Christmas\nJoin us for a wonderful day of Christmas shopping.
  This is a one-day handcrafted show. Shop for that special gift from over 
 50 craft vendors. We will have food trucks on site. Free goodie bags for t
 he first 100 groups. All bags will include vendor coupons and a chance to 
 get a $25 gift card to a local restaurant. Free parking adults $5 admissio
 n kids 12 and under free.\nBlue Ridge College Conference Hall\; 49 East Ca
 mpus Drive\; Flat Rock\,\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/southern
 -touch-craft-show-christmas-in-hendersonville\n.\n**Sat\; Nov 14**\nCaroli
 na Shag Beach dance (2nd Sat.)\n7pm to 10pm\; $7.00 per person\nAmerican L
 egion Post 77\; 216 4th Ave.W. Hendersonville\n.\n**Sat\; Nov 14**\nThe Ma
 ttocks – Johnson Band\n7-9pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust
  St\, Hendersonville\n.\n**Wed\, Nov 18**\nCarolina Shag Night - Featuring
  DJ Rick Selimos (Open to the Public)\n6-9pm\, American Legion Post 88\, 1
 15 East Morgan St\, Brevard NC 28712\n6-6:30pm - Free Shag Dance Lesson. 7
 -9pm - Dancing to DJ Rick Selimos who will be playing a mix of\nShag\, Swi
 ng\, Slow Dance and Line Dance music.\n.\n**Every Wednesday\, Nov 18**\nJa
 son DeCristofaro's Jazz Night (Each Wednesday)\n6-8pm\, Southern Appalachi
 an Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonville\n.\n**Every Wednesday\, Nov 18
 1th**\nWeekly Westie Wednesdays (Ages 21 & Up) (Each Wednesday)\n7-10pm\, 
 Honeysuckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\, Suite 101\, Hendersonville NC 287
 92\n7-8pm - Continuation Lesson & 7:30-8pm - Beginner Lesson. 8-10pm - Soc
 ial Dance.\nLessons rotate weekly with our incredible instructor lineup: R
 yan Pflumm\, Jason Barnes\, Jenna Shimek\,\nMissy Lindsey\, Rachel Harris\
 , Tom and Janet Leazenby\, and Tola Sun - all bringing fresh energy and\np
 erspectives each week! Enjoy a rotation of community DJs keeping the vibes
  high and the floor full all night\nlong. No outside drinks (including wat
 er bottles) - water station available. Outside food welcome. Dress is\ncas
 ual and No partner needed! Dedicated parking next to the venue & street pa
 rking. Please help us\nsupport our amazing host venue by grabbing a drink 
 or snack at the bar - it helps keep dance nights thriving!\nPricing: $10 l
 esson & social\, $5 social only\n.\n**Hospice Warehouse sale\; Nov 20 & 21
 . (**(3rd Fri/Sat of mnth)\nYou'll find a wide variety of value furniture 
 items at the warehouse. Shop with us each month when we host our 2-day war
 ehouse sales and support the care services of Four Seasons.\n9:00 AM - 2:0
 0 PM\; 561 S Allen Rd\, Flat Rock\nhttps://www.facebook.com/HospiceHomeSto
 re\n.\n**November 20** @ 10:00 am - 2:00 pm\; Free\nHandmade Holidays Craf
 t Fair & Market\nPurchase holiday gifts from Carolina Village residents an
 d staff\,\nin our Fireplace Lounge & Village Hall\nFree parking and free e
 ntry!\nCrafters & artists will be offering handmade:\n• Fine art\; Paper
  crafts\; Teddy bears\; Artisan Santas\; Fiber arts\; Jewelry\; Wreaths\; 
 Stationery\; Décor\; Books\;\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/event/han
 dmade-holidays-craft-fair-market\n.\n**Saturday\, November 21**\nThe Showb
 oat Band (No Cover)\n3:30-6:30pm\, Point Lookout Vineyards\, 408 Appleola 
 Road\, Hendersonville\n.\n**Saturday\, November 21**\nJohnny Blackwell & t
 he Jukebox Brothers\n7-9pm\, Guidon Brewery\, 415 8th Ave. East\, Henderso
 nville\n.\n**November 21** @ 9:00 am - 1:00 pm\nThanksgiving Holiday Marke
 t at the Hendersonville Farmers Market\n9am-1pm at the historic Train Depo
 t. It’s your chance to discover one-of-a-kind gifts\, holiday decoration
 s\, and delectable treats for your feasts. With over 30 enthusiastic vendo
 rs\, this is a can’t-miss event.\n.\n**November 21\; 10:00 am - 5:00 pm\
 ; Free**\nJeter Mountain Farm Christmas\nkeepsake hot chocolate to a holid
 ay hard cider\, live Christmas jazz music to rocking chairs around the fir
 e\,\nXmas Trees available by reservation…\nhttps://www.jetermountainfarm
 .com/attractions/christmas\n.\n**Saturday\, November 21**\nMountain Shag C
 lub Thanksgiving Party (With DJ “Big Fish” Calhoun)\n6-10pm\, Henderso
 nville Elks Lodge\, 546 North Justice St\, Hendersonville NC 28739\nManna 
 Food Bank Fundraiser – Please bring $$ or non-perishable food items to d
 onate.\nBring a snack to share and 50/50 raffle. FREE for members and $10 
 for Guests.\n.\n**Sunday\, Nov 22**\nHendersonville Ballroom Dance Club Te
 a Dance - Attire: Casual Dress\n3-5:30pm\, Upstairs at Hedrick Rhodes Vete
 rans Center\, 900 North Main St\, Hendersonville NC 28792\n3pm - Dance Les
 son.\nAmple parking at the front entry of the building\, take the elevator
  or stairs to the upper level. Parking is limited at the rear entrance\, b
 oth front and back doors will be unlocked. 3-5:30pm –\nOur dances are op
 en to the public and everyone is invited. Enjoy Ballroom Dancing to the mu
 sic of DJ Gary Bills who plays a variety of dance tunes including Swing (E
 ast & West Coast)\, Waltz\, Tango\, Rumba\, Cha-Cha and Foxtrot. There is 
 also a dance mixer Cost: $5 per person at door.\n.\nThese are NOT hosted e
 vents and are posted for informational purposes only. Please make personal
  arrangements to meetup with friends and family.\nIf you wish to attend an
 d host one of these events\, I will post the event as an individual happen
 ing. Hosting only requires being focal point for others and making introdu
 ctions. Simple!!
